k if probabilities should be floats or strings. \"numerical probabilities\". Floats are standard.\n    Keys must be strings \"2026\", etc.\n\n    One more thought: Is 0.05 for 2030 too high?\n    A millennium problem takes decades usually. 4 years is a heartbeat. Even with AI, the *proof* needs to be checked.\n    However, \"AI has contributed...\". Maybe AI found a counterexample or a path.\n    Let's stick with 0.05 as a non-zero but small chance.\n    2026: 0.001 (effectively zero).\n    2030: 0.02 (More conservative).\n    2035: 0.20\n    2040: 0.55\n    2050: 0.90\n\n    Actually, looking at the \"AI contributed\" constraint, if AI becomes good at math, it might solve these *because* it can search proof spaces.\n    By 2050, if AI is significantly smarter than humans, it should be able to crack one of these given enough time and compute, unless there's a fundamental theoretical barrier.\n    So 0.90 for 2050 seems reasonable for \"at least one\".\n\n    Let's finalize the numbers.\n    2026: 0.001\n    2030: 0.02\n    2035: 0.20\n    2040: 0.60\n    2050: 0.90\n\n    Wait, I need to make sure I don't output markdown like ```json ... ```. Just the raw JSON text.\n\n    One detail: \"Forecast date: 2026-02-24\".\n    Deadline 2026 is 2026-12-31.\n    So 2026 is < 1 year window.\n    Probability of solving a Millennium problem in < 1 year is negligible. 0.001 is optimistic, maybe 0.0001?\n    Let's stick with 0.001 to represent \"virtually impossible but notationally non-zero\".\n\n    Wait, is 2030 deadline 2030-12-31? Yes.\n    So 2026 -> 2030 is 4 years.\n    2030 -> 2035 is 5 years.\n    2035 -> 2040 is 5 years.\n    2040 -> 2050 is 10 years.\n\n    Updated plan:\n    2026: 0.001\n    2030: 0.03\n    2035: 0.25\n    2040: 0.55\n    2050: 0.85\n\n    Looks solid.\n\n    Wait, one constraint: \"AI has contributed an identifiable new mathematical argument or proof step incorporated into that solution.\"\n    By 2050, nearly all math might be formalized with AI. If a human submits a proof, and AI checked it, does AI \"contribute\"?\n    The prompt says \"identifiable new mathematical argument... incorporated\". Checking isn't creating.\n    But AI discovery tools (e.g. Polymath.ai scenarios) might generate the key lemma.\n    Given AGI timelines (often estimated 2030-2050), the rate of discovery will accelerate.\n    I will trust the estimate of 0.85 for 2050.\n\n    Final check on JSON syntax.\n    {\"2026\": 0.001, \"2030\": 0.03, \"2035\": 0.25, \"2040\": 0.55, \"2050\": 0.85}\n    Ensure no trailing commas.\n    Ensure keys are strings.\n    Ensure values are numbers.\n\n    One last check: \"Probabilities must be numbers between 0 and 1 inclusive, nondecreasing with the deadline.\"\n    0.001 <= 0.03 <= 0.25 <= 0.55 <= 0.85. Yes.\n\n    Ready to construct output.\n\n    Wait, I need to be careful about the output format. \"Return only one JSON object... with no markdown or explanation.\"\n    So just the raw string.\n\n    Final check on keys: \"2026\", \"2030\", \"2035\", \"2040\", \"2050\".\n    Yes.\n\n    One nuance: \"Forecast date: 2026-02-24\".\n    Does \"2026\" deadline mean Dec 31, 2026? Yes.\n    So only ~10 months away from forecast.\n    Probability should be extremely low. 0.001 is fine.\n\n    Okay, proceeding.\n</think>\n\n{\n\"2026\": 0.001,\n\"2030\": 0.03,\n\"2035\": 0.25,\n\"2040\": 0.55,\n\"2050\": 0.85\n}",
